<title>USA: Detroit Diesel names Leuliette vice chairman.</title>
<headline>Detroit Diesel names Leuliette vice chairman.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Detroit Diesel Corp said it named Timothy Leuliette to the newly created position of vice chairman.</p>
<p>The announcement was made by Roger Penske, chairman and chief executive officer.  Detroit Diesel, a manufacturer of diesel and alternative fuel engines, is about 46 percent owned by closely held Penske Corp, a diversified transportation services company.</p>
<p>Leuliette also recently was named president and chief operating officer and a director of Penske.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
